<body>
    <h1>AWS Polly: Languages and Voices</h1>
    <div class=3D"Section1">
        <h1 id=3D"AWSPolly:LanguagesandVoices-UsinglanguagesinLogic+">Using=
 languages in Logic+</h1>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Voice name format for variables.</strong> All voices can be refe=
renced by name directly or in variables. Voice names must be written 1) wit=
h a capital first letter and 2) without any diacritics (e.g., accents, or m=
arks, that appear over certain vowels and consonants).</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>For example, the Brazilian Portuguese voice =E2=80=9C<code>Vit=C3=B3ria<=
/code>" should be "<code>Vitoria</code>" if used in a variable. Similarly, =
the French voice =E2=80=9C<code>L=C3=A9a</code>" should be "<code>Lea</code=
>" if used in a variable.</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ul>
<h1 id=3D"AWSPolly:LanguagesandVoices-Availablelanguagesandvoices">Availabl=
e languages and voices</h1>
<div class=3D"confluence-information-macro confluence-information-macro-inf=
ormation">
<span class=3D"aui-icon aui-icon-small aui-iconfont-info confluence-informa=
tion-macro-icon"></span>
<div class=3D"confluence-information-macro-body">
<p><strong>Last updated: 12/18/2023</strong></p>
</div>
</div>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Total languages supported: 27</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>This count includes regional languages (English Australian/British/India=
n, Portuguese Brazil/European, etc.)</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ul>
